              }
            ]
          },
          "themeBinding": "warmth"
        },
        {
          "id": "explore-analogue",
          "type": "deeper",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "explore-analogue-note",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "variant": "body",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Analogue matching: we compare the city’s projected yearly mean and seasonal swing with every other city’s present values, and pick the nearest. Weighted: mean temperature counts double the seasonal swing."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "closing",
      "title": "Weather changes daily. Climate moves slowly, then all at once.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "closing-body",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "variant": "body",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Nothing here tells you what will happen. It shows what a few degrees can mean when you attach them to a place you can picture."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "demo-data-note",
          "type": "data-note",
          "lead": "Demo data, not a forecast.",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "City temperatures are rounded approximations and the warming per city is an invented illustrative rule (more at higher latitudes). Real projections depend on emissions pathways and models; for real numbers see the IPCC Sixth Assessment Report and the Köppen-Geiger maps by Beck et al. (2018, CC BY 4.0)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
